libfprint-egis0576 (1.94.100-99egis1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild of upstream libfprint v1.94.100 with the out-of-tree egis0576
    (EgisTec EH576, USB 1c7a:0576) driver compiled in. Mirrors
    packaging/fedora/libfprint.spec: same upstream version, same meson
    integration patch, same suspend/resume sleep hook and udev rule.
  * Debian revision "-99egis1" is chosen the same way the Fedora spec's
    Release: 99...egis9 is: the numeric part (99) sorts above any plausible
    normal Debian revision (-1, -2, ...) at the same upstream Version, so
    this package wins on version alone against the stock libfprint-2-2,
    libfprint-2-dev and gir1.2-fprint-2.0 it deliberately reuses the names
    of. No epoch, Provides, Conflicts or Replaces is needed as a result.

